1
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Who is Salt?

2
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Salt is a action, mystery, thriller film directed by Phillip Noyce.

3
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
As a CIA officer, Evelyn Salt swore an oath to duty, honor and country.

4
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Her loyalty will be tested when a Russian defector
accuses her of being a Russian sleeper spy.

5
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
She goes on the run, using all her skills and years of experience as a covert operative to elude
capture, protect her husband, and stay one step ahead of her colleagues at the CIA.

6
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Her efforts to prove her innocence only serve to cast doubt on her motives, as the hunt to uncover
the truth behind her identity continues and the question remains: "Who is Salt?"

7
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Evelyn Salt, played by Angelina Jolie.

8
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Theodore Winter, played by Liev Schreiber.

9
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Darryl Peabody, played by Chiwetel Ejiofor.

10
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Oleg Vasilyevich Orlov, played by Daniel Olbrychski.

11
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Mike Krause, played by August Diehl.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Young Orlov, played by Daniel Pearce.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Salt is a 2010 American action thriller film directed by
Phillip Noyce and written by Kurt Wimmer.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
It stars Angelina Jolie, Liev Schreiber, Daniel
Olbrychski, August Diehl, and Chiwetel Ejiofor.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Jolie plays CIA operative Evelyn Salt, who is accused of being a Russian
sleeper agent and goes on the run to try to clear her name.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
Originally written with a male protagonist, with Tom Cruise initially secured for the
lead, the script was ultimately rewritten by Brian Helgeland for Jolie.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Filming took place on location in Washington, D.C., New York City, and Albany, New
York, between March and June 2009, with reshoots in January 2010.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Action scenes were primarily performed with practical stunts,
computer-generated imagery being used mostly for creating digital environments.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The film had a panel at San Diego Comic-Con on July 22 and was
released in North America on July 23, 2010.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Salt grossed $294 million at the worldwide box office and received generally positive reviews, with praise for the action scenes and
Jolie's performance, but drawing criticism on the writing, with reviewers finding the plot implausible and convoluted.

21
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The DVD and Blu-ray discs were released on December 21, 2010, and featured
two alternate cuts providing different endings for the film.

22
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
Salt was nominated for Best Sound Mixing at the 83rd Academy Awards.

23
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
The film explores themes of new york city, race against time, central
intelligence agency (cia), washington dc, usa, funeral.

24
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
The tone is lighthearted and mind_bending and intense.
